🚨 **BLOCKING: CLI `/skills on|off` never republishes `_agent.operativeSkills` — a disabled skill's pins keep riding, an enabled skill's pins never start**

The PR's own derived-state contract (P2: "consent and toggle changes re-publish") is implemented at boot (`agent_cli_lifecycle.dart:156`), on reload/consent/import (`_reloadSkills`, this line), and in the app host (`setSkillToggle`, `setSkillsAccess` — `agent_service_skills.dart:217`, `agent_service_wiring.dart:148`). The CLI per-skill toggle path is missed:

```dart
// skill_commands.dart — _applySkillToggle (lines 640-641)
await _resolveSkillAvailability();   // recomputes _enabledSkills …
_applyPromptComposition();           // … but the agent's pin source set is NOT updated
```

`_createLoopConfig` reads `Agent.operativeSkills` per run, so after `/skills off fleet project` (the settings-hub Skills flow routes here — "same-session effect, no restart") the agent keeps rebuilding the pin registry from the stale list: `fleet`'s operative directives continue to be pinned verbatim into every post-compaction request and every summarization prompt. The lifecycle diff can't catch it either — the registry rebuilds from the same stale list, so it diffs clean (no drop notice). The inverse is equally silent: `/skills on fleet` mid-session never starts its pins until a full `/skills reload` or restart.

This is the same "stale/inert source set" class round 2 blocked on for the app boot path, on the toggle path of the CLI host.

Fix (mirror the reload path, or fold the republish into `_resolveSkillAvailability` itself so every recompute publishes):

```dart
if (!persisted) return;
await _resolveSkillAvailability();
// gh-1409: republish the operative-pin source set (derived state, P2) —
// the toggle changed it, same as reload/consent/import do.
_agent.operativeSkills = List.of(_enabledSkills);
_applyPromptComposition();
```

Add a regression test next to `test/cli/` (toggle a pin-owning skill off → `agent.operativeSkills` no longer contains it; on → it does), mirroring `flutter_app/test/agent_service_operative_pins_test.dart`.

